      "type": "inputNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": -190
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Robot Autonomy Execution Task",
        "nodeType": "text_input",
        "properties": {
          "message": "Execute the one high-level plannerDecision using current evidence, Robot Status, persona, recent context, and advertised capabilities. The delegated instruction is authoritative intent; current bridge facts are authoritative physical context. Choose one response, one advertised action, or one body-local movementRequest. Prefer an advertised command when its description performs the needed effect; use movementRequest only when the requested movement is not covered. Preserve body part, direction, timing, and hold details. Do not invent an unrelated idle task.\n\nReturn strict JSON: response, actions, movementRequest, and taskDecision with objective, reason, outcome, objectiveComplete, continuationPolicy, and requiredCompletionBasis. Physical work uses outcome=act and objectiveComplete=false because the result will be interpreted by Robot Action Result after this workflow ends. Outward response is optional; leave it empty when speaking adds nothing and otherwise use one or two concise sentences. Never promise an absent action.",
          "inputKey": ""
        }
      }
    },
